      "text": "To determine which of the five segments shown is the longest, we need to analyze the given angles in the figure. The angles provided are \\(55^\\circ\\), \\(55^\\circ\\), \\(40^\\circ\\), and \\(75^\\circ\\).\n\nFirst, let's identify the segments:\n- \\(AB\\)\n- \\(BC\\)\n- \\(CD\\)\n- \\(DA\\)\n- \\(BD\\)\n\nWe need to find the relationship between these segments based on the given angles. Let's assign variables to the segments:\n- Let \\(AB = x\\)\n- Let \\(BC = y\\)\n- Let \\(CD = z\\)\n- Let \\(DA = w\\)\n- Let \\(BD = u\\)\n\nGiven the angles:\n- \\(\\angle BAC = 55^\\circ\\)\n- \\(\\angle ABC = 55^\\circ\\)\n- \\(\\angle BCD = 40^\\circ\\)\n- \\(\\angle CDA = 75^\\circ\\)\n\nTo find the longest segment, we need to compare the lengths of the sides. The longest segment will be the one opposite the largest angle.\n\nLet's analyze the angles and their corresponding sides:\n- \\(\\angle BAC = 55^\\circ\\) (opposite segment \\(AB\\))\n- \\(\\angle ABC = 55^\\circ\\) (opposite segment \\(BC\\))\n- \\(\\angle BCD = 40^\\circ\\) (opposite segment \\(CD\\))\n- \\(\\angle CDA = 75^\\circ\\) (opposite segment \\(DA\\))\n\nSince \\(55^\\circ\\) is the largest angle, the segment opposite this angle will be the longest. Therefore, the longest segment is \\(DA = w\\).\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{w}\n\\]",
